commit 735f3c48c0776e62f9b0121cb8efa51ab095bec0
Author: Clément Boudereau <cboudereau@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Mar 26 17:22:33 2026 +0100

    feat(otlp-migration): step 4b — tail sampling transform
    
    Add tail_sample transform that buffers OTel spans by trace_id and evaluates
    sampling policies after a configurable decision wait. Mirrors the OTel
    Collector Contrib tailsamplingprocessor.
    
    Core features:
    - Trace buffer with LRU eviction (configurable num_traces + max_trace_size_bytes)
    - Decision wait timer (configurable seconds since first span)
    - Decision cache: separate sampled/non-sampled LRU caches for late-arriving spans
    - First-match policy evaluation
    
    Sampling policies implemented:
    - always_sample: unconditional sampling
    - status_code: match span status (OK, ERROR, UNSET)
    - latency: trace duration threshold (with optional upper bound)
    - probabilistic: CRC32 hash-based deterministic sampling
    - rate_limiting: token-bucket rate limiter
    - span_count: min/max span count per trace
    - string_attribute: match span attribute values
    - numeric_attribute: match span attribute in range
    
    10 unit tests covering policy evaluation, buffer eviction, decision cache,
    and late-arriving span handling.

