commit b115630e522d87bc33b4e653099fe11d70022730
Author: Clément Boudereau <cboudereau@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Mar 26 14:27:27 2026 +0100

    feat(otlp-migration): step 4a.3 — load-balanced OTel gRPC sink
    
    Integrate consistent-hash load balancing into the OTel gRPC sink.
    When `load_balancing` is configured, events are routed to multiple
    backends via CRC32 consistent hashing on traceID or service name.
    
    Architecture (mirrors OTel Collector Contrib loadbalancingexporter):
    - Per-backend OtlpGrpcService with independent Channel
    - Consistent hash ring routes events → backend
    - Resolver watch channel triggers ring rebuild on backend changes
    - Batch per-backend with configurable timeout, then send
    
    Config integration:
    - `load_balancing` optional field on GrpcConfig
    - When None: existing single-endpoint behavior (unchanged)
    - When Some: LoadBalancedOtlpGrpcSink routes events by key
    - All config types implement configurable_component for TOML support

