    Replace the `todo!()` panic in `VrlTarget::new()` for `Event::OtelLog`,
    `Event::OtelSpan`, and `Event::OtelMetric` with full VRL target support.
    
    OTel logs and spans use eager projection: the proto is converted to a
    `Value::Object` on construction, VRL mutates it freely, and `into_events()`
    writes changes back to the proto. OTel metrics use a restricted-path model
    (like legacy `Metric`) — only `.name`, `.description`, `.unit`, `.resource`,
    `.scope` are accessible.
    
    This unblocks all VRL-based transforms (remap, filter, route, sample,
    dedupe, exclusive_route) for OTel-native events flowing through the pipeline.
    
