    fix(otlp-migration): step 0b — preserve InstrumentationScope on spans + backpressure test
    
    Span scope fix (lib/opentelemetry-proto/src/spans.rs):
      `ResourceSpans::into_event_iter` was silently dropping the
      `InstrumentationScope` of each `ScopeSpans` group.  The scope is now
      threaded through to `ResourceSpan::into_event` and stored under
      `scope.{name,version,attributes}` on the resulting `TraceEvent`,
      mirroring the existing pattern in `logs.rs`.
      Two tests added: `scope_name_and_version_preserved` and
      `missing_scope_does_not_panic`.
    
    Per-signal backpressure isolation test (lib/vector-core/src/source_sender/tests.rs):
      `per_signal_backpressure_isolation` fills the metrics named-output channel
      to capacity (1 slot), then asserts that logs and traces can still be sent
      within 200 ms — confirming that `SourceSender::named_outputs` provides
      truly independent channels per signal type.

commit d80fe32ebb431909fcf000cd5501e9ad1b969ca6
Author: Clément Boudereau <cboudereau@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Feb 19 18:19:14 2026 +0100

    feat(otlp-migration): step 0a — disk buffer format toggle with OTLP encoding
    
    Add a process-wide `BufferFormat` toggle (`vector` / `otlp` / `migrate`)
    that controls how new disk-buffer records are serialised.
    
    - `BufferFormat` enum + `BUFFER_FORMAT: AtomicCell` in `vector-core/event/ser.rs`
    - `EventEncodableMetadataFlags::OtlpEncoding` flag: stamps OTLP records so the
      reader knows which decoder to invoke
    - `encode()` / `decode()` branch on the toggle; OTLP path calls through an
      `OtlpCodec` trait registered via `OnceLock` to avoid a circular dependency
      between `vector-core` and `opentelemetry-proto`
    - `OtlpCodec` trait + registry in `vector-core/event/otlp.rs`
    - `OtlpBufferBatch` (hand-written prost::Message) + `VectorOtlpCodec` impl in
      `opentelemetry-proto/src/buffer_codec.rs` with round-trip tests
    - `buffer_format` field added to `GlobalOptions`; startup wiring in `app.rs`
      stores the configured value and registers the codec
    
    Zero-downtime migration path: `migrate` mode writes OTLP records but reads both
    formats so existing Vector-proto records drain cleanly before the switch.

commit e487d6ed6fa413f2ced27780227424f02472c799
Author: Pavlos Rontidis <pavlos.rontidis@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Feb 19 13:36:15 2026 -0500

    fix(ci): Fix K8s E2E test failures (#24694)
    
    * fix(ci): Prevent duplicate Docker builds in test channel
    
    The build-docker.sh script was building the same image 3 times when
    CHANNEL=test and BASE is specified (e.g., BASE=debian). This happened
    because all three ${BASE:-"default"} expressions evaluated to the same
    value.
    
    Now when BASE is specified, only that base image is built once. When
    BASE is not specified, all three variants (alpine, distroless-libc,
    distroless-static) are built as before.
    
    This eliminates redundant builds in K8s E2E tests which set BASE=debian,
    reducing CI time and avoiding potential image caching issues.
    
    🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * fix(ci): Use Docker API v1.43 to work around minikube/Docker 29 incompatibility
    
    Docker 25+ (including 29.1.5 on GitHub Actions) removed the VirtualSize field
    from the image API, causing "unable to calculate manifest" errors when loading
    images into minikube.
    
    Even minikube v1.34.0 doesn't fully fix Docker 29 compatibility. Using
    DOCKER_API_VERSION=1.43 forces Docker to use the older API that includes
    VirtualSize, allowing minikube to successfully load images.
    
    This is a known issue tracked in moby/moby#47207. While not the most elegant
    solution, it's currently the most reliable workaround for Docker 29 + minikube
    compatibility issues.
    
    🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * update linked issue
    
